---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Lauren Chaplinski, data engineer and architect transitioning from consulting into independent contract work."
>
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-24 sm:pt-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink mb-8">
      About
    </h1>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        I'm a data engineer and architect. 12+ years working specifically with
        healthcare data, most recently Medicaid rate-setting, supplemental
        payment calculations and administration, and federal compliance
        demonstrations for state agencies, as a Managing Consultant at a large
        consulting firm. That depth is in the data, not the policy: I'm not
        the person who writes the regulation, I'm the person whose pipeline
        has to prove the state complied with it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Underneath that specific expertise is 8 years building production data
        systems: data lakes, pipelines, cloud migrations, in Python, SQL,
        SAS, and Azure. That's the part that generalizes. A schema mistake or
        a broken pipeline has compliance consequences in this world, not just
        a bad dashboard, and I've come to think of that as the real training
        ground: the habits that hold up there hold up anywhere, regardless of
        industry.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm now transitioning from consulting into independent contract work. The
        engineering doesn't change: I'm still designing pipelines, running cloud
        migrations, and modeling data that has to be right the first time. What
        changes is who I build it for, and how directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of client work, I build things because I want them to exist: a
        synthetic data generator, a self-hosted multiplayer game, a home automation
        stack that runs on the same instincts as everything else I build: contained,
        automated, and not held together with duct tape.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <a
        href="/resume.pdf"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded bg-ink text-paper font-medium text-sm hover:bg-accent-strong transition-colors"
      >
        View résumé
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-faint mt-10">$ cat about.md</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
